    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Less than a kilometre from the centre of Cannes, the Croix des Gardes forest offers 80 hectares of pine woods and shaded trails, a real breath of fresh air a stone's throw from the Croisette.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The official leaflet of the city of Cannes on the Croix-des-Gardes nature park (municipal order no. 09616, April 2016) says dogs may be walked off-leash, except on the fitness trail where a leash is required (aggressive or dangerous-category dogs excepted). The site is a sensitive natural area owned by the Conservatoire du littoral; any breach of the rules is punishable by a €135 fine. This leaflet dates from 2016 and the city's page does not detail the rules for dogs: if in doubt, ask Cannes' green spaces department (04 89 82 24 40). Also keep in mind that in woods and forests, national regulations require a leash outside the paths from 15 April to 30 June.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the fitness trail is well marked on site — look for the signs to know where to put the leash back on.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Central Cannes and the Croisette can be reached on foot from several entrances to the forest.</p>
